title start
kind: default
tags: test editor introduction
A Welcome to AIU EDITOR: an introduction that is also a test page
title end

comment start
Every key in this page works in the visual layer unless a part says otherwise. The mode line at the bottom shows where you are, for example visual general.
comment end

paragraph start
This page teaches the editor and tests it at once. You are looking at a page drawn as boxes. One block is lit at a time, and the keys below move it, edit it and pick what it moves between. Read a part, press the keys it names, and see the lit block change.
paragraph end

section start
title start
1. Moving between blocks
title end

paragraph start
Press t to light the next block and h to light the one before it. The page scrolls to follow the lit block. Try it now: walk down this section and back up.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Space n jumps to the next block and space e to the end of the block. Space u shows more rows of the editor.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Sections nest
title end

paragraph start
This paragraph sits in a section inside a section. The drawing numbers sections for you, and h and t walk into nested sections in page order.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Three levels deep
title end

paragraph start
The deepest level in this page. If the lit block here matches the box you see, the level by level matching works.
paragraph end
section end
section end
section end

section start
title start
2. Picking what h and t move between
title end

paragraph start
Plain keys pick the kind of block. They change nothing but the pick, and h and t stay the movement keys. The mode line shows it, for example visual navigation [todo open].
paragraph end

code start
language: text
a  any block (back to visual general)
p  paragraph
e  section
c  code
k  comment
l  title
x  any todo
o  open todo
d  done todo
code end

paragraph start
Try it: press c and then t. Only the code blocks of this page are visited. Press a to go back to every block.
paragraph end

comment start
Press k and walk: only comments are lit. Press l and walk: only titles are lit.
comment end
section end

section start
title start
3. Todos
title end

paragraph start
todo: open press o, then t, and see that only open todos are visited
An open todo is drawn in red with a tray under its box.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: open press w on this block, change this line, then press escape to save
The first word after todo: is the state: open or done.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: press x and see that a todo with no word counts as open
No word after the colon means open.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: done press d and see that this done todo is visited
A done todo has no red.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: open the cursor cannot land on the todo tray after a block move
This is a known bug, kept here as a real open todo.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
4. Editing
title end

paragraph start
Press w to edit the lit block as raw text, with its start and end lines. Press i to edit only its text inside the box. Escape saves and returns to visual general.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Space f opens the whole page as text, the write layer. There the tab key is the trigger: tab s saves, tab b lists the blocks, tab tab switches layer and escape leaves.
paragraph end

code start
language: text
w          edit the block raw
i          edit the text of the block
backspace  delete one character
escape     save and leave
space s    save
space f    write the whole page
code end
section end

section start
title start
5. Moving blocks
title end

paragraph start
Press m to move the lit block. Then h and t swap it with the sibling before or after it, and escape ends the move. Titles and answers never move.
paragraph end

paragraph start
This paragraph is a good one to move. Press m, then t twice, then escape.
paragraph end

paragraph start
And this one is its neighbour. It should swap places with the one above.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Press n and s to move the point left and right inside the block.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
6. The bar, the tabs and finding
title end

paragraph start
Space b opens the bar keys: where the bar stands, how it looks and which parts it shows. Space t opens the tab keys: the tabs, the project row and the workspace row. Space z hides everything and brings it back.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Space / finds with fzf: f for this file, p for the project, w for the workspace, then t for text, b for blocks, d for todos, n for files. A pick opens as a tab at the right line.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Press space and wait: a popup lists the modes you can switch to and the keys that can follow.
paragraph end

code start
language: text
space b  bar keys
space t  tab keys
space z  focus: hide or show the bars
space /  find with fzf
space ?  explorer
space k  check the page
space g  send
space q  quit
code end
section end

section start
title start
7. The home screen
title end

paragraph start
Start aiutd with no file and the home screen lists your pages. The keys 1 to 9 open that page, and space q quits.
paragraph end

code start
language: nu
aiutd test.aiu
aiutd
code end
section end

comment start
End of the introduction. Press space k to check this page: a page that checks clean is a good sign for the whole editor.
comment end
